sentences.text:
that the present appeal is devoid of merits and same has been filed just to cause the delay in execution of the sentence awarded by the Ld. M.M.;
that the appellant miserably failed to point out any irregularity or infirmity in the impugned judgments; that the Ld. M.M. has passed the reasoned orders; that the argument of the appellant that Ld. MM has passed sentence of seven months is vague since he is sentenced only for four months and in default he was sentenced to undergo three months imprisonment; that Ld. MM had given opportunity to the appellant to cross examine the complainant and to lead defence evidence hence the Ld. Trial Court did not commit any illegality; that in the civil suit for specific performance filed by the complainant/respondent for execution of sale deed and handover the possession of the property, the appellant CA No. 204120/2016 Jiauddin Vs. Yamin Khan & Anr. PAGE NO. 5 OF 16 has categorically stated that he paid Rs.9,00,000/- out of Rs.13,00,000/- to the respondent; that the said suit has been decreed in favour of the complainant for the recovery of amount which has been challenged in appeal but since appellant did not deposit the decreetal amount as ordered by the Hon'ble High Court, stay qua the same was vacated; that the appellant has failed to rebut the presumption whereas complainant has proved his case by leading cogent evidence; that no suggestion was put to the complainant regarding the fact that he was not able to pay Rs.9,00,000/-;
that the case of the appellant is that he put his signatures on the blank cheques but his signatures are also there on the revenue stamp; that appellant further admitted that he handed over chain of his ownership document to the complainant which proves that the agreement for sell was actually executed; that the witnesses brought by the appellant failed to rebut the case as they had not deposed when the document and cheques were taken and they deposed that no help was provided by them when appellant's son met with an accident; that they are also inconsistent on the amount spent on the treatment; that the impugned judgment does not suffer from any illegality or infirmity and appellant has been rightly convicted.

At the stage of the recording of statement of accused, accused took the plea that he procured loan of Rs.2,00,000/- from the complainant; that " as a security towards the repayment of the said loan, the complainant require him to deliver six blank cheques which he accordingly issued and delivered;
that the complainant also required him to sign a blank stamp paper and another blank paper, which he accordingly signed and delivered the same to the complainant; that the CA No. 204120/2016 Jiauddin Vs. Yamin Khan & Anr. PAGE NO. 8 OF 16 complainant sought interest @ 15% per month on the said loan; that he endavoured to deliberate upon a settlement with the complainant but he Jiauddin vs Yamin Khan And Anr on 14 May, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/71922566/
4 instead presented the blank cheques delivered by him for payment and initiated the present prosecution against him to extort money from him."

He has deposed that "My son met with an accident in May 2010; that after that period of five days he was shifted to my residence; that when he was shifted home, a number of people had come to ask about his CA No. 204120/2016 Jiauddin Vs. Yamin Khan & Anr. PAGE NO.
13 OF 16 wellness; that the complainant had also come home to inquire about my son's illness; that the complainant offered monetary help as assistance as I was in need of money; that I was in need of money as such I accepted his offer; that the complainant gave me Rs. Two Lakhs by way of cash;
that I had given him six blank cheques and one stamp paper in blank and also one blank plan paper signed by me; that I had given the said cheques and stamp paper and plane paper as security; that the complainant used to provide finance assistance to the people on interest basis; that there was no talks for the sale of said property where I was residing.

